Investigate whether a normally installed CLUE application uses the real Symcor and Tungsten endpoints during operational batch execution, or can silently run against fixtures, replay data, loopback/local services, or simulators.

This is a separate read-only investigation. Do not implement or repair anything.

Use English for all engineering output.

Critical distinction

Do not equate these two concepts:

* installer --dry-run versus real installation;
* application offline/fixture mode versus live-provider mode.

A non-dry-run installation should install and validate the application without contacting providers. Real Symcor/Tungsten requests should occur only later, when the installed operational batch is intentionally run in live mode.

The investigation must determine whether the supported post-install operational command selects live providers safely.

Read-only boundaries

* Do not edit, create, delete, restore, format, stage, or rewrite files.
* Do not commit, push, fetch, merge, rebase, stash, reset, clean, checkout, tag, or update a PR.
* Do not build, install, publish, deploy, or mutate /app/clue.
* Do not run a non-dry-run installer.
* Do not call live Symcor, Tungsten, Salt, Vault, Nexus, or any other external service.
* Do not retrieve or expose secrets.
* Do not request the owner’s password.
* Report findings in chat only.

