Installer behavior

Inspect dry-run and non-dry-run installation paths separately.

Prove whether each path performs any of these actions:

* provider-client construction;
* Symcor/Tungsten network request;
* fixture execution;
* secret retrieval;
* certificate validation;
* wrapper smoke test;
* configuration-only validation.

Expected safe behavior:

* installer dry-run: no mutation, no secret retrieval, no provider request;
* installer non-dry-run: installation and local validation only, with no business/provider request;
* operational batch run: provider calls only when explicitly and validly configured for live mode.

Report deviations, but do not change them.

