A prior screenshot showed provider_mode: fixtures in dev.yaml. Determine whether that is still true in the exact current snapshot and whether the operational wrapper overrides it.

Do not expose query strings, tokens, keys, passwords, certificate bodies, or private paths. Endpoint hostnames and configuration-key names are sufficient.

PAT and Production tungsten_base_url values may remain UNCONFIRMED. Do not guess them. Treat them as external live-readiness gaps.

Provider implementation inspection

Identify the concrete implementations selected for each mode.

For Symcor, determine whether runtime can select:

* real SOAP/TLS client;
* fixture reader;
* replay client;
* local simulator;
* mock/test client.

For Tungsten, determine whether runtime can select:

* real HTTP/TLS client;
* fixture OCR result reader;
* replay client;
* loopback/local service;
* mock/test client.

Search for silent fallback logic such as:

try live provider
on failure use fixtures/replay/mock

Any such fallback in installed DEV/PAT/Production execution must be reported explicitly.

A provider failure should not silently produce simulated business results.

