Tests

Inspect tests covering:

* dry-run never contacts providers;
* non-dry-run installation never performs a business/provider call;
* installed operational execution selects live mode;
* fixtures require explicit offline/local selection;
* missing provider mode fails closed in installed execution;
* missing live endpoint fails closed;
* missing live credential fails closed;
* Symcor/Tungsten modes cannot diverge unintentionally;
* provider failure does not fall back to fixtures;
* direct Python invocation cannot bypass the installed provider-mode contract;
* logs identify live versus fixture mode safely;
* fake cheque data cannot be returned during an intended live execution.

Do not claim tests passed solely because test files exist. Separate test definitions from executed evidence.

Do not run any test capable of contacting a real provider. Narrow synthetic unit tests may run only if they use temporary directories, explicit mocks, and cannot interfere with the implementation session.

